{"step_index":325,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T18:10:49Z","input_tokens":2130,"cache_read_tokens":224625,"output_tokens":14542,"thinking":"User requires a comprehensive, plot-ready CSV export of all substage timings from testing for thesis data analysis. This necessitates careful CSV design to include all relevant time data points with appropriate headers for direct plotting in common tools. The goal is to ensure the CSV structure is directly usable without pre-processing for plotting and analysis.\n\n\nInitial CSV design prioritizes two files for maximum plotting flexibility. The first, `thesis_summary_results.csv`, will aggregate performance statistics for each test scenario. This file will include metadata and all time data points for provisioning and deployment sub-stages. A second file is likely also needed to support micro-phase level data from the Deployment sub-stage.\n\n\n`thesis_summary_results.csv` must include all deployment sub-stage timing metrics, focusing on average, p50, and p95 percentiles for creation, pushing, starting, runtime network, and database recording. Also include the total standard deviation of deployment time.\n\nFor sub-stage 3 (OVN sandbox verification), extract and include all macro and micro-phase verification timings such as total wall time, average total time, and percentile values, along with setup, OVN network creation, CoW clone, and clone connection times. These will form the second CSV file.\n\n\nThe second CSV file, `thesis_raw_samples.csv`, will require a unique row for each team's execution within each tier and cycle. This granular data structure enables detailed visualizations like boxplots, violin plots, and CDFs. Key verification substage metrics, including clone start, clone runtime, runner execution, readiness checks, command execution, and cleanup times (average, p50, and p95), will be included.\n\nTeardown substage timings, such as wall time, machine teardown, team teardown, and individual team teardown metrics (average, p95), will be incorporated into the raw sample data. RAM usage metrics—baseline, after deployment, after verification, and after teardown—are critical for understanding resource consumption and will also be tracked within the raw data.\n\n\nRaw sample data CSV structure confirmed. Identified required columns for per-team timings and test metadata. Deployment and verification sub-stage timings are included. Need to confirm and incorporate individual container-level timings from the responses.\n\n\nConsidering that detailed container-level timings are available, the CSV structure should be expanded. Plan to generate a tier-level summary, a raw team samples CSV, a Markdown report, and a JSON state file. The summaries will now include the per-container timing data and RAM usage.\n\nDecided to construct the updated benchmark script locally, copy it to the remote server, and then show the user the anticipated CSV column structure. The detailed CSV column structures will be displayed to the user.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"Append":false,"CodeContent":"import argparse\nimport asyncio\nimport csv\nimport json\nimport logging\nimport math\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\n# Ensure blueagent and tests are importable\nsys.path.insert(0, '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src')\nsys.path.insert(0, '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent')\nos.environ['BLUEAGENT_CTFD_API_TOKEN'] = 'secret-token'\n\nfrom blueagent.engine.incus import IncusEngine\nfrom tests.usability.client import BlueAgentTestClient\n\nlogging.basicConfig(\n    level=logging.INFO,\n    format='%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(message)s',\n    datefmt='%H:%M:%S'\n)\nlogger = logging.getLogger('benchmark')\n\nSTATE_JSON_PATH = '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/thesis_stress_test_state.json'\nCSV_SUMMARY_PATH = '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/thesis_stress_test_results.csv'\nCSV_RAW_SAMPLES_PATH = '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/thesis_raw_team_samples.csv'\nREPORT_OUTPUT_PATH = '/home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/tests/thesis_stress_test_report.md'\n\n\ndef percentile(data: List[float], p: float) -> float:\n    if not data:\n        return 0.0\n    sorted_data = sorted(data)\n    k = (len(sorted_data) - 1) * (p / 100.0)\n    f = math.floor(k)\n    c = math.ceil(k)\n    if f == c:\n        return round(sorted_data[int(k)], 4)\n    d0 = sorted_data[int(f)] * (c - k)\n    d1 = sorted_data[int(c)] * (k - f)\n    return round(d0 + d1, 4)\n\n\ndef calculate_stats(values: List[float]) -> Dict[str, float]:\n    if not values:\n        return {'avg': 0.0, 'p50': 0.0, 'p95': 0.0, 'min': 0.0, 'max': 0.0, 'std': 0.0}\n    avg = sum(values) / len(values)\n    variance = sum((x - avg) ** 2 for x in values) / len(values)\n    return {\n        'avg': round(avg, 4),\n        'p50': percentile(values, 50),\n        'p95': percentile(values, 95),\n        'min': round(min(values), 4),\n        'max': round(max(values), 4),\n        'std': round(math.sqrt(variance), 4),\n    }\n\n\ndef get_system_metrics() -> Dict[str, int]:\n    mem_total, mem_avail = 0, 0\n    try:\n        with open('/proc/meminfo', 'r') as f:\n            for line in f:\n                if line.startswith('MemTotal:'):\n                    mem_total = int(line.split()[1]) // 1024\n                elif line.startswith('MemAvailable:'):\n                    mem_avail = int(line.split()[1]) // 1024\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    used_ram = mem_total - mem_avail\n    return {'used_ram_mb': used_ram, 'free_ram_mb': mem_avail}\n\n\ndef build_challenge_payload(team_k: int, num_containers: int) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    containers = []\n    verify_commands = []\n    for i in range(num_containers):\n        c_name = f'app{i+1}'\n        containers.append({\n            'name': c_name,\n            'image': 'alpine',\n            'ip_suffix': i + 2,\n            'limits_cpu': '1',\n            'limits_memory': '128MB'\n        })\n        verify_commands.append({\n            'target': 'container',\n            'container_name': c_name,\n            'cmd': ['echo', f'verified_{c_name}'],\n            'timeout': 15,\n            'interval': 1,\n            'retry_timeout': 10\n        })\n\n    return {\n        'challenge_id': f'ch-bench-{team_k}',\n        'team_k': team_k,\n        'containers': containers,\n        'readiness_commands': [],\n        'verify_commands': verify_commands,\n        'verify_internet_access': False\n    }\n\n\nclass BenchmarkRunner:\n    def __init__(self, base_url: str = 'http://127.0.0.1:8000', token: str = 'secret-token'):\n        self.client = BlueAgentTestClient(base_url=base_url, token=token, timeout=900.0)\n        self.results: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n        self.raw_samples: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n\n    def load_existing_state(self):\n        path = Path(STATE_JSON_PATH)\n        if path.exists():\n            try:\n                data = json.loads(path.read_text())\n                self.results = data.get('results', [])\n                self.raw_samples = data.get('raw_samples', [])\n                logger.info('Loaded %d existing tier results and %d raw samples from %s',\n                            len(self.results), len(self.raw_samples), STATE_JSON_PATH)\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.warning('Could not load state file %s: %s', STATE_JSON_PATH, e)\n\n    def upsert_result(self, tier_res: Dict[str, Any], tier_samples: List[Dict[str, Any]]):\n        test_name = tier_res['test_name']\n        self.results = [r for r in self.results if r.get('test_name') != test_name]\n        self.results.append(tier_res)\n\n        self.raw_samples = [s for s in self.raw_samples if s.get('test_name') != test_name]\n        self.raw_samples.extend(tier_samples)\n\n        # Immediately flush all outputs so no progress is ever lost\n        self.save_state_json()\n        self.export_summary_csv()\n        self.export_raw_samples_csv()\n        self.export_markdown_report()\n\n    def save_state_json(self, filename: str = STATE_JSON_PATH):\n        Path(filename).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        with open(filename, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump({'results': self.results, 'raw_samples': self.raw_samples}, f, indent=2)\n\n    async def ensure_clean_environment(self, team_ids: List[int]):\n        \"\"\"Parallel cleanup of BlueAgent teams + direct Incus sweep of any orphaned verify-* resources.\"\"\"\n        logger.info('Performing parallel pre-flight cleanup for teams: %s', team_ids)\n\n        async def _clean_team(k: int):\n            try:\n                await self.client.teardown_challenge(team_k=k)\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            try:\n                await self.client.delete_team(team_k=k)\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n\n        await asyncio.gather(*[_clean_team(k) for k in team_ids])\n\n        # Sweep any orphaned verify-* containers or OVN networks directly via Incus UDS\n        engine = IncusEngine(socket_path='/var/lib/incus/unix.socket')\n        try:\n            instances = await engine.list_instances()\n            orphan_insts = [\n                inst.get('name', '') for inst in instances\n                if inst.get('name', '').startswith('verify-') or inst.get('name', '').startswith('c-')\n            ]\n            if orphan_insts:\n                logger.warning('Sweeping %d orphaned Incus instances: %s', len(orphan_insts), orphan_insts)\n                await asyncio.gather(*[\n                    engine.delete_instance(name, force=True) for name in orphan_insts\n                ], return_exceptions=True)\n\n            networks = await engine.list_networks()\n            orphan_nets = [\n                net.get('name', '') for net in networks\n                if net.get('name', '').startswith('verify-')\n            ]\n            if orphan_nets:\n                logger.warning('Sweeping %d orphaned OVN networks: %s', len(orphan_nets), orphan_nets)\n                await asyncio.gather(*[\n                    engine.delete_network(name) for name in orphan_nets\n                ], return_exceptions=True)\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.warning('Incus orphan sweep warning: %s', e)\n        finally:\n            await engine.aclose()\n\n    async def _timed_create_team(self, k: int, name: str) -> Tuple[int, float, int]:\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        r = await self.client.create_team(team_k=k, name=name)\n        return k, round(time.perf_counter() - t0, 4), r.status_code\n\n    async def _timed_deploy(self, k: int, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[int, float, httpx.Response]:\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        r = await self.client.deploy_challenge(payload, team_k=k)\n        return k, round(time.perf_counter() - t0, 4), r\n\n    async def _timed_verify(self, k: int, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[int, float, httpx.Response]:\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        r = await self.client.verify_challenge(team_k=k, config_payload=payload)\n        return k, round(time.perf_counter() - t0, 4), r\n\n    async def _timed_teardown_machines(self, k: int) -> Tuple[int, float, int]:\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        r = await self.client.teardown_challenge(team_k=k)\n        return k, round(time.perf_counter() - t0, 4), r.status_code\n\n    async def _timed_delete_team(self, k: int) -> Tuple[int, float, int]:\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        r = await self.client.delete_team(team_k=k)\n        return k, round(time.perf_counter() - t0, 4), r.status_code\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Core Execution of a Single (M, N) Scenario or Cycle\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    async def execute_barrier_scenario(\n        self,\n        test_name: str,\n        test_type: str,\n        m: int,\n        n: int,\n        cycle_idx: Optional[int] = None,\n        clean_before: bool = True,\n    ) -> Tuple[Dict[str, Any], List[Dict[str, Any]]]:\n        team_ids = list(range(1, m + 1))\n        if clean_before:\n            await self.ensure_clean_environment(team_ids)\n\n        ram_baseline = get_system_metrics()['used_ram_mb']\n\n        # SUB-STAGE 1: Provision M Teams in parallel & wait\n        t_prov_start = time.perf_counter()\n        prov_results = await asyncio.gather(*[\n            self._timed_create_team(k, f'{test_name} Team {k}')\n            for k in team_ids\n        ])\n        prov_wall_sec = round(time.perf_counter() - t_prov_start, 4)\n        prov_times_map = {k: elapsed for k, elapsed, _ in prov_results}\n\n        # SUB-STAGE 2: Deploy M x N Containers in parallel & wait\n        payloads = {k: build_challenge_payload(team_k=k, num_containers=n) for k in team_ids}\n        t_dep_start = time.perf_counter()\n        dep_results = await asyncio.gather(*[\n            self._timed_deploy(k, payloads[k])\n            for k in team_ids\n        ])\n        dep_wall_sec = round(time.perf_counter() - t_dep_start, 4)\n        ram_after_deploy = get_system_metrics()['used_ram_mb']\n\n        # Short settle pause so ZFS/network state stabilizes before Verify burst\n        await asyncio.sleep(1.0)\n\n        # SUB-STAGE 3: Verify M Teams in parallel & wait\n        t_ver_start = time.perf_counter()\n        ver_results = await asyncio.gather(*[\n            self._timed_verify(k, payloads[k])\n            for k in team_ids\n        ])\n        ver_wall_sec = round(time.perf_counter() - t_ver_start, 4)\n        ram_after_verify = get_system_metrics()['used_ram_mb']\n\n        # SUB-STAGE 4: Teardown all M x N containers & M teams in parallel & wait\n        t_tear_start = time.perf_counter()\n        t_mach_start = time.perf_counter()\n        tear_mach_results = await asyncio.gather(*[\n            self._timed_teardown_machines(k)\n            for k in team_ids\n        ])\n        tear_machines_wall_sec = round(time.perf_counter() - t_mach_start, 4)\n\n        t_team_start = time.perf_counter()\n        tear_team_results = await asyncio.gather(*[\n            self._timed_delete_team(k)\n            for k in team_ids\n        ])\n        tear_teams_wall_sec = round(time.perf_counter() - t_team_start, 4)\n        teardown_wall_sec = round(time.perf_counter() - t_tear_start, 4)\n        ram_after_teardown = get_system_metrics()['used_ram_mb']\n\n        tear_mach_map = {k: elapsed for k, elapsed, _ in tear_mach_results}\n        tear_team_map = {k: elapsed for k, elapsed, _ in tear_team_results}\n\n        # Parse per-team metrics\n        dep_map = {k: (elapsed, r) for k, elapsed, r in dep_results}\n        ver_map = {k: (elapsed, r) for k, elapsed, r in ver_results}\n\n        raw_rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n        errors: List[str] = []\n        pass_count = 0\n\n        for k in team_ids:\n            prov_sec = prov_times_map[k]\n            dep_http_sec, r_dep = dep_map[k]\n            ver_http_sec, r_ver = ver_map[k]\n            tm_sec = tear_mach_map[k]\n            tt_sec = tear_team_map[k]\n\n            dep_st = {}\n            if r_dep.status_code in (200, 201):\n                dep_st = r_dep.json().get('step_timings', {})\n            else:\n                errors.append(f'Team {k} Deploy HTTP {r_dep.status_code}: {r_dep.text[:120]}')\n\n            ver_st = {}\n            sb = {}\n            cl = {}\n            ver_passed = False\n            if r_ver.status_code == 200:\n                v_json = r_ver.json()\n                ver_passed = bool(v_json.get('passed'))\n                if ver_passed:\n                    pass_count += 1\n                ver_st = v_json.get('details', {}).get('step_timings', {})\n                sb = ver_st.get('sandbox_setup', {})\n                cl = ver_st.get('cleanup', {})\n            else:\n                errors.append(f'Team {k} Verify HTTP {r_ver.status_code}: {r_ver.text[:150]}')\n                logger.error('[%s] Team %d verify error: %s', test_name, k, r_ver.text[:200])\n\n            row = {\n                'test_name': test_name,\n                'test_type': test_type,\n                'teams_m': m,\n                'containers_n': n,\n                'cycle': cycle_idx if cycle_idx is not None else 1,\n                'team_k': k,\n                'http_deploy_status': r_dep.status_code,\n                'http_verify_status': r_ver.status_code,\n                'verify_passed': int(ver_passed),\n                # Sub-stage 1: Provision\n                'provision_team_sec': prov_sec,\n                # Sub-stage 2: Deploy\n                'deploy_http_sec': dep_http_sec,\n                'deploy_total_sec': dep_st.get('total_deploy_sec', dep_http_sec),\n                'deploy_validation_sec': dep_st.get('validation_sec', 0.0),\n                'deploy_create_sec': dep_st.get('total_create_sec', 0.0),\n                'deploy_push_sec': dep_st.get('total_push_sec', 0.0),\n                'deploy_start_sec': dep_st.get('total_start_sec', 0.0),\n                'deploy_runtime_net_sec': dep_st.get('total_runtime_net_sec', 0.0),\n                'deploy_db_record_sec': dep_st.get('total_db_record_sec', 0.0),\n                # Sub-stage 3: Verify\n                'verify_http_sec': ver_http_sec,\n                'verify_total_sec': ver_st.get('total_verify_lifecycle_sec', ver_http_sec if r_ver.status_code == 200 else 0.0),\n                'verify_setup_total_sec': sb.get('total_setup_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_ovn_net_create_sec': sb.get('ovn_network_create_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_cow_clone_sec': sb.get('total_clone_time_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_clone_connect_sec': sb.get('total_connect_time_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_clone_start_sec': sb.get('total_start_time_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_clone_runtime_net_sec': sb.get('total_runtime_net_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_runner_sec': sb.get('verifier_runner_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_readiness_sec': ver_st.get('readiness_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_commands_sec': ver_st.get('verify_commands_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_cleanup_clones_sec': cl.get('clones_teardown_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_cleanup_ovn_net_sec': cl.get('ovn_network_delete_sec', 0.0),\n                'verify_cleanup_total_sec': cl.get('total_cleanup_sec', 0.0),\n                # Sub-stage 4: Teardown\n                'teardown_machines_sec': tm_sec,\n                'teardown_team_sec': tt_sec,\n                'teardown_total_sec': round(tm_sec + tt_sec, 4),\n            }\n            raw_rows.append(row)\n\n        summary = self._aggregate_rows_to_summary(\n            test_name=test_name,\n            test_type=test_type,\n            m=m,\n            n=n,\n            cycles=1,\n            raw_rows=raw_rows,\n            prov_wall_sec=prov_wall_sec,\n            dep_wall_sec=dep_wall_sec,\n            ver_wall_sec=ver_wall_sec,\n            tear_machines_wall_sec=tear_machines_wall_sec,\n            tear_teams_wall_sec=tear_teams_wall_sec,\n            teardown_wall_sec=teardown_wall_sec,\n            ram_baseline=ram_baseline,\n            ram_after_deploy=ram_after_deploy,\n            ram_after_verify=ram_after_verify,\n            ram_after_teardown=ram_after_teardown,\n            errors=errors,\n        )\n        return summary, raw_rows\n\n    def _aggregate_rows_to_summary(\n        self,\n        test_name: str,\n        test_type: str,\n        m: int,\n        n: int,\n        cycles: int,\n        raw_rows: List[Dict[str, Any]],\n        prov_wall_sec: float,\n        dep_wall_sec: float,\n        ver_wall_sec: float,\n        tear_machines_wall_sec: float,\n        tear_teams_wall_sec: float,\n        teardown_wall_sec: float,\n        ram_baseline: int,\n        ram_after_deploy: int,\n        ram_after_verify: int,\n        ram_after_teardown: int,\n        errors: List[str],\n    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        ok_dep = [r for r in raw_rows if r['http_deploy_status'] in (200, 201)]\n        ok_ver = [r for r in raw_rows if r['http_verify_status'] == 200 and r['verify_passed'] == 1]\n        total_attempts = len(raw_rows)\n        passed_count = len(ok_ver)\n        failed_count = total_attempts - passed_count\n\n        def col_stats(rows: List[Dict[str, Any]], key: str) -> Dict[str, float]:\n            return calculate_stats([float(r[key]) for r in rows])\n\n        return {\n            'test_name': test_name,\n            'test_type': test_type,\n            'teams_count': m,\n            'containers_per_team': n,\n            'cycles': cycles,\n            'total_containers_live': m * n,\n            'peak_containers_verify': 2 * m * n,\n            'passed_count': passed_count,\n            'failed_count': failed_count,\n            'passed_ratio': f'{passed_count}/{total_attempts}',\n            'pass_rate_pct': round((passed_count / total_attempts) * 100.0, 2) if total_attempts else 0.0,\n            # Wall-clock times per barrier sub-stage\n            'provision_wall_sec': prov_wall_sec,\n            'deploy_wall_sec': dep_wall_sec,\n            'verify_wall_sec': ver_wall_sec,\n            'teardown_machines_wall_sec': tear_machines_wall_sec,\n            'teardown_teams_wall_sec': tear_teams_wall_sec,\n            'teardown_wall_sec': teardown_wall_sec,\n            # Macro stats\n            'provision_stats': col_stats(raw_rows, 'provision_team_sec'),\n            'deploy_stats': col_stats(ok_dep, 'deploy_total_sec'),\n            'verify_stats': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_total_sec'),\n            'teardown_machines_stats': col_stats(raw_rows, 'teardown_machines_sec'),\n            'teardown_team_stats': col_stats(raw_rows, 'teardown_team_sec'),\n            'teardown_total_stats': col_stats(raw_rows, 'teardown_total_sec'),\n            # Micro-phase stats\n            'phase_stats': {\n                # Deploy micro-phases\n                'deploy_validation_sec': col_stats(ok_dep, 'deploy_validation_sec'),\n                'deploy_create_sec': col_stats(ok_dep, 'deploy_create_sec'),\n                'deploy_push_sec': col_stats(ok_dep, 'deploy_push_sec'),\n                'deploy_start_sec': col_stats(ok_dep, 'deploy_start_sec'),\n                'deploy_runtime_net_sec': col_stats(ok_dep, 'deploy_runtime_net_sec'),\n                'deploy_db_record_sec': col_stats(ok_dep, 'deploy_db_record_sec'),\n                # Verify micro-phases\n                'verify_setup_total_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_setup_total_sec'),\n                'ovn_create_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_ovn_net_create_sec'),\n                'cow_clone_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_cow_clone_sec'),\n                'clone_connect_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_clone_connect_sec'),\n                'clone_start_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_clone_start_sec'),\n                'clone_runtime_net_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_clone_runtime_net_sec'),\n                'verify_runner_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_runner_sec'),\n                'verify_readiness_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_readiness_sec'),\n                'verify_cmds_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_commands_sec'),\n                'cleanup_clones_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_cleanup_clones_sec'),\n                'cleanup_ovn_net_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_cleanup_ovn_net_sec'),\n                'cleanup_sec': col_stats(ok_ver, 'verify_cleanup_total_sec'),\n            },\n            # Memory snapshots across barriers\n            'ram_baseline_mb': ram_baseline,\n            'ram_after_deploy_mb': ram_after_deploy,\n            'ram_after_verify_mb': ram_after_verify,\n            'ram_after_teardown_mb': ram_after_teardown,\n            'ram_used_mb': ram_after_verify,\n            'errors': errors,\n        }\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # TEST 1: Single-Team Baseline & Micro-Phase Profiling\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    async def run_test_1(self, cycles: int = 10):\n        logger.info('===============================================================')\n        logger.info('TEST 1: SINGLE-TEAM BASELINE & MICRO-PHASE PROFILING (M=1, N=1, %d cycles)', cycles)\n        logger.info('===============================================================')\n\n        await self.ensure_clean_environment([1])\n        all_cycle_rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n        all_errors: List[str] = []\n        prov_walls, dep_walls, ver_walls, tm_walls, tt_walls, tear_walls = [], [], [], [], [], []\n        ram_base_list, ram_dep_list, ram_ver_list, ram_tear_list = [], [], [], []\n\n        for c in range(1, cycles + 1):\n            logger.info('[Test 1] Cycle %d/%d starting...', c, cycles)\n            summary_c, rows_c = await self.execute_barrier_scenario(\n                test_name='Test 1 (Baseline M=1, N=1)',\n                test_type='test_1_baseline',\n                m=1,\n                n=1,\n                cycle_idx=c,\n                clean_before=False,\n            )\n            all_cycle_rows.extend(rows_c)\n            all_errors.extend(summary_c['errors'])\n            prov_walls.append(summary_c['provision_wall_sec'])\n            dep_walls.append(summary_c['deploy_wall_sec'])\n            ver_walls.append(summary_c['verify_wall_sec'])\n            tm_walls.append(summary_c['teardown_machines_wall_sec'])\n            tt_walls.append(summary_c['teardown_teams_wall_sec'])\n            tear_walls.append(summary_c['teardown_wall_sec'])\n            ram_base_list.append(summary_c['ram_baseline_mb'])\n            ram_dep_list.append(summary_c['ram_after_deploy_mb'])\n            ram_ver_list.append(summary_c['ram_after_verify_mb'])\n            ram_tear_list.append(summary_c['ram_after_teardown_mb'])\n            logger.info('[Test 1] Cycle %d/%d finished: Prov=%.3fs, Deploy=%.3fs, Verify=%.3fs, Teardown=%.3fs',\n                        c, cycles, summary_c['provision_wall_sec'], summary_c['deploy_wall_sec'],\n                        summary_c['verify_wall_sec'], summary_c['teardown_wall_sec'])\n\n        final_summary = self._aggregate_rows_to_summary(\n            test_name='Test 1 (Baseline M=1, N=1)',\n            test_type='test_1_baseline',\n            m=1,\n            n=1,\n            cycles=cycles,\n            raw_rows=all_cycle_rows,\n            prov_wall_sec=round(sum(prov_walls) / len(prov_walls), 4),\n            dep_wall_sec=round(sum(dep_walls) / len(dep_walls), 4),\n            ver_wall_sec=round(sum(ver_walls) / len(ver_walls), 4),\n            tear_machines_wall_sec=round(sum(tm_walls) / len(tm_walls), 4),\n            tear_teams_wall_sec=round(sum(tt_walls) / len(tt_walls), 4),\n            teardown_wall_sec=round(sum(tear_walls) / len(tear_walls), 4),\n            ram_baseline=int(sum(ram_base_list) / len(ram_base_list)),\n            ram_after_deploy=int(sum(ram_dep_list) / len(ram_dep_list)),\n            ram_after_verify=int(sum(ram_ver_list) / len(ram_ver_list)),\n            ram_after_teardown=int(sum(ram_tear_list) / len(ram_tear_list)),\n            errors=all_errors,\n        )\n        self.upsert_result(final_summary, all_cycle_rows)\n        logger.info('[+] Test 1 Completed and flushed to CSV/Markdown.')\n        return final_summary\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # TIERED STRESS TEST MATRIX (Also covers Test 3 on N=2 slice)\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    async def run_tiered_matrix(self, teams: List[int], containers: List[int]):\n        logger.info('===============================================================')\n        logger.info('TIERED STRESS TEST MATRIX (M in %s, N in %s)', teams, containers)\n        logger.info('===============================================================')\n\n        for m in teams:\n            for n in containers:\n                test_name = f'Tier M={m} N={n}'\n                logger.info('>>> STARTING TIER: M=%d teams, N=%d containers/team (Peak Instances: %d) <<<',\n                            m, n, 2 * m * n)\n                summary, raw_rows = await self.execute_barrier_scenario(\n                    test_name=test_name,\n                    test_type='matrix_and_test3' if n == 2 else 'matrix',\n                    m=m,\n                    n=n,\n                    cycle_idx=1,\n                    clean_before=True,\n                )\n                self.upsert_result(summary, raw_rows)\n                logger.info(\n                    '[+] Completed %s (Pass=%s): ProvWall=%.3fs, DeployWall=%.3fs, VerifyWall=%.3fs (p95=%.3fs), TeardownWall=%.3fs, RAM=%dMB',\n                    test_name, summary['passed_ratio'], summary['provision_wall_sec'],\n                    summary['deploy_wall_sec'], summary['verify_wall_sec'],\n                    summary['verify_stats']['p95'], summary['teardown_wall_sec'],\n                    summary['ram_after_verify_mb']\n                )\n\n        # Final cleanup sweep\n        max_m = max(teams) if teams else 15\n        await self.ensure_clean_environment(list(range(1, max_m + 1)))\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # CSV & Markdown Exporters\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def export_summary_csv(self, filename: str = CSV_SUMMARY_PATH):\n        Path(filename).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        headers = [\n            'test_name', 'test_type', 'teams_m', 'containers_per_team_n', 'cycles',\n            'live_containers', 'peak_verify_containers', 'passed_count', 'failed_count', 'pass_rate_pct',\n            # Sub-stage 1: Provisioning\n            'provision_wall_sec', 'provision_team_avg_sec', 'provision_team_p50_sec', 'provision_team_p95_sec',\n            'provision_team_min_sec', 'provision_team_max_sec', 'provision_team_std_sec',\n            # Sub-stage 2: Deployment Macro\n            'deploy_wall_sec', 'deploy_total_avg_sec', 'deploy_total_p50_sec', 'deploy_total_p95_sec',\n            'deploy_total_min_sec', 'deploy_total_max_sec', 'deploy_total_std_sec',\n            # Sub-stage 2: Deployment Micro-phases\n            'deploy_validation_avg_sec',\n            'deploy_create_avg_sec', 'deploy_create_p50_sec', 'deploy_create_p95_sec',\n            'deploy_push_avg_sec', 'deploy_push_p50_sec', 'deploy_push_p95_sec',\n            'deploy_start_avg_sec', 'deploy_start_p50_sec', 'deploy_start_p95_sec',\n            'deploy_runtime_net_avg_sec', 'deploy_runtime_net_p50_sec', 'deploy_runtime_net_p95_sec',\n            'deploy_db_record_avg_sec',\n            # Sub-stage 3: Verification Macro\n            'verify_wall_sec', 'verify_total_avg_sec', 'verify_total_p50_sec', 'verify_total_p95_sec',\n            'verify_total_min_sec', 'verify_total_max_sec', 'verify_total_std_sec',\n            # Sub-stage 3: Verification Micro-phases\n            'verify_setup_total_avg_sec', 'verify_setup_total_p50_sec', 'verify_setup_total_p95_sec',\n            'verify_ovn_create_avg_sec', 'verify_ovn_create_p50_sec', 'verify_ovn_create_p95_sec',\n            'verify_cow_clone_avg_sec', 'verify_cow_clone_p50_sec', 'verify_cow_clone_p95_sec',\n            'verify_clone_connect_avg_sec', 'verify_clone_connect_p50_sec', 'verify_clone_connect_p95_sec',\n            'verify_clone_start_avg_sec', 'verify_clone_start_p50_sec', 'verify_clone_start_p95_sec',\n            'verify_clone_runtime_net_avg_sec', 'verify_clone_runtime_net_p50_sec', 'verify_clone_runtime_net_p95_sec',\n            'verify_runner_avg_sec', 'verify_readiness_avg_sec',\n            'verify_cmds_avg_sec', 'verify_cmds_p50_sec', 'verify_cmds_p95_sec',\n            'verify_cleanup_clones_avg_sec', 'verify_cleanup_ovn_net_avg_sec',\n            'verify_cleanup_total_avg_sec', 'verify_cleanup_total_p50_sec', 'verify_cleanup_total_p95_sec',\n            # Sub-stage 4: Teardown\n            'teardown_machines_wall_sec', 'teardown_teams_wall_sec', 'teardown_wall_sec',\n            'teardown_machines_avg_sec', 'teardown_machines_p95_sec',\n            'teardown_team_avg_sec', 'teardown_team_p95_sec',\n            'teardown_total_avg_sec', 'teardown_total_p95_sec',\n            # Memory (MB)\n            'ram_baseline_mb', 'ram_after_deploy_mb', 'ram_after_verify_mb', 'ram_after_teardown_mb',\n        ]\n        with open(filename, 'w', newline='') as f:\n            writer = csv.writer(f)\n            writer.writerow(headers)\n            for r in self.results:\n                ps = r.get('phase_stats', {})\n                prov_s = r.get('provision_stats', {})\n                dep_s = r.get('deploy_stats', {})\n                ver_s = r.get('verify_stats', {})\n                tm_s = r.get('teardown_machines_stats', {})\n                tt_s = r.get('teardown_team_stats', {})\n                ttot_s = r.get('teardown_total_stats', {})\n\n                writer.writerow([\n                    r.get('test_name'),\n                    r.get('test_type'),\n                    r.get('teams_count'),\n                    r.get('containers_per_team'),\n                    r.get('cycles', 1),\n                    r.get('total_containers_live'),\n                    r.get('peak_containers_verify'),\n                    r.get('passed_count'),\n                    r.get('failed_count'),\n                    r.get('pass_rate_pct'),\n                    # Sub-stage 1\n                    r.get('provision_wall_sec'),\n                    prov_s.get('avg', 0), prov_s.get('p50', 0), prov_s.get('p95', 0),\n                    prov_s.get('min', 0), prov_s.get('max', 0), prov_s.get('std', 0),\n                    # Sub-stage 2 Macro\n                    r.get('deploy_wall_sec'),\n                    dep_s.get('avg', 0), dep_s.get('p50', 0), dep_s.get('p95', 0),\n                    dep_s.get('min', 0), dep_s.get('max', 0), dep_s.get('std', 0),\n                    # Sub-stage 2 Micro\n                    ps.get('deploy_validation_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_create_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_create_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_create_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_push_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_push_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_push_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_start_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_start_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_start_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_runtime_net_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_runtime_net_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_runtime_net_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('deploy_db_record_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    # Sub-stage 3 Macro\n                    r.get('verify_wall_sec'),\n                    ver_s.get('avg', 0), ver_s.get('p50', 0), ver_s.get('p95', 0),\n                    ver_s.get('min', 0), ver_s.get('max', 0), ver_s.get('std', 0),\n                    # Sub-stage 3 Micro\n                    ps.get('verify_setup_total_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('verify_setup_total_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('verify_setup_total_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('ovn_create_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('ovn_create_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('ovn_create_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('cow_clone_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('cow_clone_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('cow_clone_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_connect_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_connect_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_connect_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_start_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_start_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_start_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_runtime_net_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_runtime_net_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('clone_runtime_net_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('verify_runner_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('verify_readiness_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('verify_cmds_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('verify_cmds_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('verify_cmds_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    ps.get('cleanup_clones_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('cleanup_ovn_net_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('cleanup_sec', {}).get('avg', 0),\n                    ps.get('cleanup_sec', {}).get('p50', 0),\n                    ps.get('cleanup_sec', {}).get('p95', 0),\n                    # Sub-stage 4 Teardown\n                    r.get('teardown_machines_wall_sec'),\n                    r.get('teardown_teams_wall_sec'),\n                    r.get('teardown_wall_sec'),\n                    tm_s.get('avg', 0), tm_s.get('p95', 0),\n                    tt_s.get('avg', 0), tt_s.get('p95', 0),\n                    ttot_s.get('avg', 0), ttot_s.get('p95', 0),\n                    # RAM\n                    r.get('ram_baseline_mb', 0),\n                    r.get('ram_after_deploy_mb', 0),\n                    r.get('ram_after_verify_mb', 0),\n                    r.get('ram_after_teardown_mb', 0),\n                ])\n        logger.info('[+] Exported Summary CSV (%d rows) to %s', len(self.results), filename)\n\n    def export_raw_samples_csv(self, filename: str = CSV_RAW_SAMPLES_PATH):\n        Path(filename).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        if not self.raw_samples:\n            return\n        headers = list(self.raw_samples[0].keys())\n        with open(filename, 'w', newline='') as f:\n            writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=headers)\n            writer.writeheader()\n            writer.writerows(self.raw_samples)\n        logger.info('[+] Exported Raw Samples CSV (%d rows) to %s', len(self.raw_samples), filename)\n\n    def export_markdown_report(self, filename: str = REPORT_OUTPUT_PATH):\n        Path(filename).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        now_str = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC')\n        with open(filename, 'w') as f:\n            f.write('# BlueAgent System Stress & Scalability Benchmark Report\\n\\n')\n            f.write(f'*Generated on:* `{now_str}` on AMD Ryzen 7 7700X (8 Cores), 15 GiB RAM\\n\\n')\n\n            f.write('## 1. Macro Sub-Stage Timings (Provision, Deploy, Verify, Teardown)\\n\\n')\n            f.write('| Scenario | M | N | Peak Cts | Pass | Prov Wall (s) | Deploy Wall (s) | Deploy p95 (s) | Verify Wall (s) | Verify p95 (s) | Teardown Wall (s) | RAM Verify (MB) |\\n')\n            f.write('| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n')\n            for r in self.results:\n                f.write(\n                    f\"| {r.get('test_name')} | {r.get('teams_count')} | {r.get('containers_per_team')} \"\n                    f\"| {r.get('peak_containers_verify')} | {r.get('passed_ratio')} \"\n                    f\"| {r.get('provision_wall_sec')} | {r.get('deploy_wall_sec')} | {r.get('deploy_stats', {}).get('p95')} \"\n                    f\"| {r.get('verify_wall_sec')} | {r.get('verify_stats', {}).get('p95')} \"\n                    f\"| {r.get('teardown_wall_sec')} | {r.get('ram_after_verify_mb')} |\\n\"\n                )\n\n            f.write('\\n## 2. Micro-Phase Breakdown (Averages per Team in Seconds)\\n\\n')\n            f.write('| Scenario | Dep Create | Dep Push | Dep Start | Dep Net | OVN Create | CoW Clone | Clone Connect | Clone Start | Clone Net | Verify Cmds | Cleanup |\\n')\n            f.write('| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n')\n            for r in self.results:\n                ps = r.get('phase_stats', {})\n                f.write(\n                    f\"| {r.get('test_name')} \"\n                    f\"| {ps.get('deploy_create_sec', {}).get('avg', 0)} \"\n                    